# Code owners of the website repository.
#
# GitHub reads this file when "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled on
# master: a pull request can only be merged once a member of an owning team of
# EVERY file it touches has approved it. The author of a pull request can
# never approve it.
#
# Review bots (cursor[bot], coderabbitai[bot]) are GitHub Apps, not members of
# these teams: their approval never satisfies this file.
#
# Last matching pattern wins. Everything belongs to the maintainers, and only
# two areas are opened to the core team:
#   - the files regenerated by the "Refresh external integrations" workflow,
#     so that its weekly pull request ("chore: refresh the external
#     integrations catalog") can be merged without the maintainers;
#   - the documentation of integrations, scenes, dashboard and development,
#     with the sidebar that lists it, the counterpart of what core merges in
#     the Gladys repository.
# A pull request that touches anything else, including one pushed on top of
# the refresh branch by hand, still needs a maintainer.
#
# The website is deployed on every merge to master, unlike Gladys, which
# waits for a release: the documentation of a feature is merged once the
# Gladys release that ships it is published, not before.
#
# Teams are referenced by slug, and a team only counts as a code owner when it
# has explicit write access (or more) to this repository. The teams are
# described in the MAINTAINERS.md file of the Gladys repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Default: maintainers only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                                   @GladysAssistant/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Generated by scripts/load_external_integrations.js and build.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The script itself and the workflow stay maintainers-only (layer 1): they
# decide what these files contain.
/src/data/externalIntegrations.json                 @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/docs/integrations/external/                        @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/i18n/fr/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/integrations/external/ @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
# Refreshed by build.sh during the same run, so it lands in the same pull
# request.
/src/data/devActivity.json                          @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Documentation: integrations, scenes, dashboard, development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installation (commands copied by users, entry pages of the website), Gladys
# Plus and the API (data model) stay maintainers-only (layer 1).
/docs/integrations/                                 @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/docs/scenes/                                       @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/docs/dashboard/                                    @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/docs/dev/                                          @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/i18n/fr/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/integrations/ @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/i18n/fr/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/scenes/ @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/i18n/fr/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/dashboard/ @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
/i18n/fr/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/dev/ @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
# A new page is listed in the sidebar, so the pull request adding it also
# edits this file. It is JavaScript run at build time: review it as code.
/sidebars.js                                        @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
# Screenshots of the documentation, shared by every section.
/static/img/docs/                                   @GladysAssistant/core @GladysAssistant/maintainers
